    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Official cause_code is 'D' per block 13, but FORM-366 category field is 'TBD/provisional' and left as such since only cause_code was authoritatively coded (category field literally reads 'provisional' in the source FORM-366 FIELDS block, so it is copied verbatim per rule 4 despite the narrative supporting a maintenance/PM-program theme). AFW/CA system actuation was an expected automatic response to the trip, not a backup restoring an inoperable HPCI-type function, so modeled as MITIGATED_BY rather than BACKED_UP_BY. No previous similar occurrence found per licensee's own 3-year review -> no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted. RPS and ESFAS described in Background as design context for how the trip functions, but RPS is the system whose actuation is itself the reportable event (50.73(a)(2)(iv)(B)), so it is retained as an INVOLVES system; ESFAS is retained only as a System node without INVOLVES since it did not itself actuate/participate in the failure chain -- included since it was named as part of the (a)(2)(iv)(B)-cited system set, but not connected via INVOLVES to avoid overstating participation."
}